 :lesson/sections
 [{:section/type :accuracy-pointer,
   :section/id 12,
   :section/title "Goofy Synergy Verb Patterns",
   :section/body
   ["Goofy pattern is the technical term for irregular verbs."
    "Notice this pattern I can Puedo You can puede But we can podemos Notice the different pattern for - we can."
    "I used to say, \"puedemos\" for about 3 years. Fortunately people understood what I meant. But you can avoid this error right away with a little attention. Just remember when you say we can - make sure to use podemos."]}
  {:section/type :communication-multiplied,
   :section/id 12,
   :section/title "You want to see us",
   :section/body
   ["In Spanish there are two ways to say, \"you want to see us.\" Do you remember?"
    "Quiere verlo you want to see him Quiere verla you want to see her Quiere verme you want to see me Here is the pattern to say you want to see us"
    "Method 1 us you want to see nos quiere ver Or you can use the easier method and attach nos to the Brick Verb."
    "Method 2 Quiere vernos you want to see us Familiar ground again. Continue using method 2, it's a faster path to communicate in Spanish."]}],
